  "content": {
    "text": "96\n\n Some risks aren\u2019t in the P&L\u2014they\u2019re in the fine print.\n\n The Sneaky Clause That Can Sink Your Deal\nHi Sara,\nEver read a contract and thought, \u201cThis is so bad it might actually be brilliant\u201d?\nA while back, I was reviewing a purchase agreement where the seller\u2019s reps and warranties did not survive the closing. As in\u2014once the ink was dry, the buyer had zero legal recourse for anything the seller promised. Nada. Zilch. No take-backs.\nHere\u2019s the twist:\n\nI was representing the seller.\n\nAnd if the buyer\u2019s team wants to skip over indemnification like it\u2019s optional reading? I\u2019m not in the business of saving people from themselves.\nBut if you\u2019re buying a business?\n\nYou need to know how indemnification works\u2014and why it\u2019s a bigger deal than most people realize.\nBecause not every risk shows up in the P&L.\n\nSome of them are buried in the fine print. And they only reveal themselves when something goes sideways.\nI recorded a video that breaks this all down:\n \u2014 What indemnification really means\n \u2014 When it matters most\n \u2014 And how to avoid the most common buyer-side mistakes\nWatch the breakdown here.\nIf you\u2019re deep in diligence or negotiating a purchase agreement right now, give it a watch.\nAnd if the indemnity language has your eyes crossing? You know where to find me.\nTo smarter contracts,\nSara Sharp\nPartner, SK&S Law Group\nFounder, Deal Academy\n\n For more helpful lessons from Deal Academy, check out our Dealmakers Youtube Channel where you'll find Sara's Weekly Wine Down, where she talks about what she's seen in the industry this week and interviews with M&A Experts and Dealmakers.\nYou can check out some recent Dealmakers YouTube videos by clicking the images below.\n\n Copyright \u00a9 2025\u00a0 Someday Consultants, All rights reserved. \n\n Our e-mail address is:\ninfo@dealacademy.org\n\n Want to change how you receive these emails?\n You can unsubscribe from this list.",
